  {"date": "2025-09-17", "venue": "Ameris Bank Amphitheatre", "city": "Alpharetta", "state": "GA", "gap": 4, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Segueing -> out of a phenomenal \"Carini,\" Trey and Page waste no time getting the band back to jamming in one of the strongest second sets of the entire year. Around 6:30 the band breaks off via isolated playing which hears Trey and Page mimic each other with bright chords while Mike and Fish offer staccato beats to create space for the jam. Trey deepens the overall exploration around 11:20 via his expert use of the synth pedal. Moving through watery tones the band explores an uptempo zone before pushing towards a truly stunning and explosive peak full of sirens and heavy Fish playing before a -> back into \"Carini.\" We're in a strong period for \"Light,\" and this version is right there with some of the finest they've ever played.", "out": ">", "prev": "Carini", "in": ">", "next": "Carini", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2025-12-30", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 6, "set": "2", "out": ">", "prev": "Ruby Waves", "in": ">", "next": "Crosseyed and Painless", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2026-01-30", "venue": "Moon Palace", "city": "Cancun", "state": "Quintana Roo", "gap": 4, "set": "2", "out": "->", "prev": "Carini", "in": ">", "next": "Frankie Says", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2026-04-17", "venue": "Sphere", "city": "Las Vegas", "state": "NV", "gap": 2, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "A swift pivot from the standard towards upbeat, blissful play opens the portal before shifting towards introspective melodic minor key territory. Page\u2019s dominating presence via both electric piano and wobbly synths then coaxes the jam towards psychedelia, as Fishman\u2019s tribalistic rhythms grow a bit more complex, gradually coalescing into a thick psychedelic groove-fest. After the 13:00 mark, the music puddles into an almost hellishly dense/atonal soundscape, eventually forming up into a driving attack before once again oscillating back towards soundscape-y madness. One last push for a full band groove eventually fades back into \u201cLight\u2019s\u201d chorus to end.", "prev": "No Men In No Man's Land", "in": ">", "next": "Joy", "nb": 1},
